{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.45,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D26", "D42", "D43", "R22", "R30", "R80"],
      "pins": ["D26.2", "D42.2", "D43.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0160", "/NET0031", "/NET0143", "/NET0111"],
      "observed": "The anodes of three LEDs (D26, D42, D43) sit on a net (/NET0160) that has no other connection. Nothing ties it to +3V3, +5V, or any driver. Their cathodes go through R22, R30 and R80 to the CM4 Ethernet/activity LED nets.",
      "expected": "The LED anodes should be tied to a supply rail (for example +3V3) so that the active-low nLED outputs of the CM4 can sink current and light the LEDs.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"37\") (name \"/NET0160\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D26\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D42\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D43\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The three status LEDs cannot be powered and will stay dark, so Ethernet/activity indication is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R59"],
      "pins": ["R59.1", "R59.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R59 is labelled 24k, but its own library description and MPN describe a 24 Ω 5% 0805 part (FRC0805J240TSD). A 24 Ω part is rated only 125 mW.",
      "expected": "A resistor across the 12 V-class output (VOUTN–VOUTP) with a 125 mW 0805 rating should be a high-value bleed (24 kΩ), consistent with the stated value and MPN agreeing.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R59\") (value \"24k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(property (name \"MPN\") (value \"FRC0805J240TSD\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If 24 Ω was intended in practice, the output would be heavily loaded and the 125 mW part would overheat. If 24 kΩ is intended, the value is consistent, so the mismatch is a labelling or BOM error.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["D27", "R28"],
      "pins": ["D27.2", "D27.4", "R28.1", "R28.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0094", "Net-(D27-K2)"],
      "observed": "The second LED channel of the dual LED D27 has its anode (A2, pin 4) on /NET0094. Its cathode (K2, pin 2) goes through R28 back to /NET0094, so the LED is effectively across a single node and carries no current. The first channel (K1 via R88) returns to GND, which suggests R28's far end should be GND.",
      "expected": "The K2 cathode resistor should return to ground, as the K1 path does with R88, so the LED is driven from /NET0094 when that line is active.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"D27\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"J14\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R28\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R28 Net-_D27-K2_ NET0094 130"}
      ],
      "impact": "The LED channel tied to /NET0094 never lights, and the resistor is connected across the drive line without serving as a limiter.",
      "confidence": 0.2
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows no clear supply short or bridged bus, but three local inconsistencies stand out: LED anodes on /NET0160 float with no supply connection, R59's value (24k) contradicts its 24 Ω MPN and description, and one D27 LED channel has its cathode resistor returned to the anode net. Confidence is moderate because these could also be original design choices."
}

